claude <claude@p7x.dev> writes:

> SigNoz is an open source observability platform. It brings logs,
> metrics, and traces together in one application, with dashboards,
> alerts, exceptions, and service maps. It is native to OpenTelemetry and
> stores its data in ClickHouse.
>
> This is the Community Edition of the query service and web interface.
> Telemetry reaches ClickHouse through the SigNoz distribution of the
> OpenTelemetry Collector, which is packaged separately.
>
> WWW: https://signoz.io/
> ---
> Notes for review:
>
> Build: on the base commit below, with Go 1.27.2 and STRICT_DEPENDS
> set, fetch ran into an empty DISTDIR with the network up. Then, as in
> a poudriere jail, DISTDIR was made read-only and the network was cut
> by pointing HTTP_PROXY and HTTPS_PROXY at a closed port. extract,
> patch, build, stage, and check-plist all passed, and go logged no
> download after fetch. vendor/modules.txt lists sonic v1.15.4 and
> sonic/loader v0.5.2. The staged binary, run as an unprivileged user
> with no ClickHouse, started its HTTP servers and ran without a panic
> until stopped. portclippy, portfmt, and portlint are clean. Not
> checked: a real poudriere build, aarch64, and a run as the signoz user
> from rc.d (that needs root).
>
> sonic: signoz v0.145.0 pins github.com/bytedance/sonic v1.14.1. Its
> map code is limited to Go 1.24 and 1.25, so it does not compile with
> the tree's Go 1.26 or 1.27, and v0.146.0 and main still pin it. The
> port raises sonic to v1.15.4 and sonic/loader to v0.5.2.
>
> How the bump is fetched: go.mk's go-post-fetch downloads the modules
> of upstream's go.mod into the module cache, GOPATH under
> ${DISTDIR}/go/net-mgmt_signoz, with the network up and every module
> checked against sum.golang.org. go-post-extract then tidies and
> vendors from that cache with GOPROXY=file://, offline. Neither knows
> about the bumped versions. So post-fetch prints upstream's go.mod with
> the two requirements raised into a mktemp(1) directory, runs the same
> "go mod download -x all" there with the same GO_ENV, and removes the
> directory. The bumped modules land in the same cache, verified the
> same way. post-extract makes the same edit to go.mod in WRKSRC, where
> the port's sources belong, and go-post-extract vendors them.
>
> Nothing in DISTDIR is written but the module cache, which go.mk
> already writes in this phase. Extract runs the fetch target again
> (_EXTRACT_DEP= fetch in bsd.port.mk), and poudriere runs it as the
> build user, offline, with DISTDIR not writable (common.sh, build_port:
> only fetch runs as root with the network). That re-run of post-fetch
> only reads the cache, exactly as go-post-fetch's own re-run does; the
> read-only test above runs this path. www/comentario fetches an extra
> module the same way, from a scratch module in post-fetch.
>
> mmap: sonic/loader v0.5.2 maps memory with MAP_ANON and fd 0.
> FreeBSD requires fd -1 and returns EINVAL, so the built binary
> panicked at startup. Upstream fixed this in bytedance/sonic commit
> bf12ab8, "MAP_ANON should be set to -1 , not required on Linux,
> required on BSD. + go fmt", merged on 2026-09-26. No sonic or loader
> release includes it yet. The port fetches that commit as a PATCHFILE
> from GitHub. It touches only loader/mmap_unix.go, and the file is the
> same in loader/v0.5.2 and in the commit's parent, so the patch applies
> cleanly. The patch can be dropped once signoz requires a loader
> release with the fix.
>
> Active query log: the PromQL engine keeps queries.active in
> prometheus.active_query_tracker.path, which defaults to "", the
> working directory. Under rc.d that is /, which the signoz user cannot
> write, so the engine panics. post-patch points the default at
> /var/db/signoz in the source and in example.yaml.
>
> Makefile, line by line:
> - MASTER_SITES and DISTFILES (:web): the web interface comes prebuilt
>   from upstream's release tarball, since the pnpm build has no offline
>   path in the tree. The source maps are left out because they make up
>   31 MB of its 54 MB and only browser developer tools read them.
> - LICENSE_FILE: installs upstream's license with the package.
> - PATCH_SITES and PATCHFILES: upstream's sonic mmap fix, fetched from
>   GitHub in fetch like any distfile and checksummed in distinfo.
> - ONLY_FOR_ARCHS: upstream releases only amd64 and arm64.
>   modernc.org/sqlite has no FreeBSD support on powerpc64 or riscv64.
> - GO_BUILDFLAGS: variant and version appear in "signoz -v" and the
>   startup log. "-s -w" is dropped because INSTALL_PROGRAM already
>   strips the binary.
> - SUB_FILES: pkg-message names %%DATADIR%%.
> - PATCH_WRKSRC: the upstream patch names paths in the sonic
>   repository (a/loader/mmap_unix.go), and go.mk vendors that repository
>   at vendor/github.com/bytedance/sonic. The port has no other patches,
>   so moving the patch directory affects only this one.
> - USERS and GROUPS: rc.d runs signoz as this user, which owns
>   /var/db/signoz.
> - SONIC_EDIT: one command for both edits, the scratch go.mod in fetch
>   and go.mod in WRKSRC, so they cannot drift.
> - The *_PROXY lines in post-fetch: SETENVI clears the environment, so
>   a fetch behind a proxy needs them passed on; go-post-fetch passes
>   the same six.
>
> UIDs/GIDs: signoz takes 485, beside prometheus 478, alertmanager 479,
> and promxy 481.
>
> Changes in v6:
> - Stop writing an edited go.mod into DIST_SUBDIR. post-fetch now
>   downloads the bumped modules from an edited go.mod in a temporary
>   directory, so the only state it leaves is the module cache go.mk
>   already fills. Pat rejected the write-on-change guard as a hack.
